   <section xreflabel="SerialDevice"
            role="class"
            xml:id="org.osgi.service.serial.SerialDevice">
      <title>public abstract SerialDevice</title>
      <para>
SerialDevice is a service representing a device performing serial
 communication.
   </para>
      <formalpara role="parameter">
         <title>Concurrency</title>
         <para>Thread-safe </para>
      </formalpara>
      <section xreflabel="DEVICE_CATEGORY"
               role="field"
               xml:id="org.osgi.service.serial.SerialDevice.DEVICE_CATEGORY">
         <title>public static final String DEVICE_CATEGORY = "Serial"</title>
         <para>
Constant for the value of the service property {@code DEVICE_CATEGORY}
 used for all Serial devices.
 
 </para>
         <para>
 A Serial base driver bundle must set this property key.</para>
         <formalpara role="parameter">
            <title>See Also</title>
            <para>
               <link linkend="UNRESOLVED">org.osgi.service.device.Constants.DEVICE_CATEGORY</link>
            </para>
         </formalpara>
      </section>
      <section xreflabel="SERIAL_COMPORT"
               role="field"
               xml:id="org.osgi.service.serial.SerialDevice.SERIAL_COMPORT">
         <title>public static final String SERIAL_COMPORT = "serial.comport"</title>
         <para>
Service property for the serial comport.
 </para>
         <para>
 Represents the name of the port. The value type is String.
 </para>
         <para>
 For example, "/dev/ttyUSB0", "COM5", or "/dev/tty.usbserial-XXXXXX".</para>
      </section>
